From 80ecce8086ae31445530f374d9a05a98de2a0fa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:20:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zeo_i18n: a translation catalog for Zeo's own screens
 (Fluent, t!, ui_language)

Zed has no UI translation at all: no i18n crate, no translatable-string
macro, no UI-language setting (checked at c31063a0; upstream has only
tracking issue #7409 and a maintainer's RFC, discussion #43592). This adds
the infrastructure for translating the screens Zeo itself adds -- Agent
Sandbox, Secrets, the task and question cards, /btw -- without touching any
of Zed's own strings, which stay English (docs/I18N-PROPOSAL.md in
zeo-workspace, phase 1). Nothing is translated by this patch: the shipped
catalogs hold no message yet, so it changes nothing anyone sees.

The design follows the RFC so the work can move onto Zed's own system if one
lands: Fluent (.ftl) files and a macro taking a stable message id,
t!("agent-sandbox-hide-host") or t!("...-jails", count = n), with a
tooltip or note addressed as an attribute, t!("id.tooltip"). Plurals and
variants live in the .ftl, never in code.

- crates/zeo_i18n: fluent-bundle's concurrent bundle, one per language in
  the chain fluent-langneg negotiates, always ending in en-US, so a message
  missing from a translation shows in English. The catalog is a process
  global, so t! needs no cx; a missing id renders as itself and is logged
  once (t! runs every frame). Isolation marks are off: GPUI draws FSI/PDI as
  boxes in some fonts and no shipped language is right-to-left.
- The .ftl files are embedded with include_str!, not rust-embed: a handful of
  small files, no path resolved at run time, a missing file fails the build.
- ui_language (top-level setting, default null): a BCP 47 tag; null follows
  the system's languages (sys-locale, already in the tree for time_format).
  Changing it rebuilds the catalog and refreshes every window, no restart.
  "en-XA" is a pseudo-locale -- en-US accented and padded by a third, in
  brackets, variables untouched -- reachable only by name so a system set to
  another English never lands on it.
- zed's main calls zeo_i18n::init after which_key, before any window opens.

New crates in Cargo.lock: fluent-bundle 0.16.0, fluent-langneg 0.13.1,
fluent-syntax 0.12.0, intl-memoizer 0.5.3, intl_pluralrules 7.0.2,
type-map 0.5.1, unic-langid 0.9.6, unic-langid-impl 0.9.6 -- all
Apache-2.0 OR MIT; rustc-hash 2, smallvec, self_cell, tinystr 0.8,
thiserror 2 and memchr were already there. UNGROUPED: every screen patch
that translates its strings depends on it, under whatever USE flag gates
that screen, so it sits with the unconditional patches, right after 0154.
---

